<https://asd.gsfc.nasa.gov/archive/ircatalog/constel_names.html>
    dcterms:title "Three-Letter Constellation Abbreviations" ;
    dcterms:creator "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, Astrophysics Science Division" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/ — “NASA content – images, audio, video, and media files used in the rendition of 3-dimensional models, such as texture maps and polygon data in any format – generally are not subject to copyright in the United States.” and “NASA content used in a factual manner that does not imply endorsement may be used without needing explicit permission. NASA should be acknowledged as the source of the material.” The page is a work of the US government (NASA/GSFC); it is used here only to verify facts. That guideline speaks of media files; for this text table it is applied by analogy: the table is a work of the US government (17 U.S.C. §105). The page’s own footer link “Privacy Policy & Important Notices” (http://www.nasa.gov/about/highlights/HP_Privacy.html, which now redirects to https://www.nasa.gov/privacy/) was fetched on 2026-10-04 and contains no copyright statement."@en .

