    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Own work of the deck's compiler, dedicated to the public domain together with the deck: the deck's dcterms:license is https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ (CC0 1.0 Universal). The equations themselves are laws of physics and definitions of quantities, which are not copyrightable; the wording of the fronts and notes, the choice of symbols and the selection are this dossier's own. The verification script is recorded verbatim under Queries."@en .

<https://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1>
    dcterms:title "University Physics, Volumes 1–3 (OpenStax)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel J. Ling, Jeff Sanny, William Moebs and contributing authors; OpenStax, Rice University" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Footer of every page fetched, e.g. https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-3-newtons-second-law (fetched 2026-10-04): \"© Jun 11, 2026 OpenStax. Textbook content produced by OpenStax is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License.\" and \"Except where otherwise noted, textbooks on this site are licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY NC-SA) license\"; the book records of all three volumes in the OpenStax archive (query 5) give the licence http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/. A non-commercial licence does not allow reuse in a CC0 deck and the builder has no identifier for CC BY-NC-SA, so the source is recorded as all-rights-reserved: verification only."@en .

