<https://history.house.gov/Institution/Presidents-Coinciding/Presidents-Coinciding/>
    dcterms:title "Presidents, Vice Presidents, & Coinciding Sessions of Congress" ;
    dcterms:creator "Office of the Historian and Office of Art & Archives (Office of the Clerk), U.S. House of Representatives" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A work of the United States Government, prepared by House staff (the Office of the Historian and the Office of the Clerk) in their official duties: 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The site gives no licence of its own; its Rights and Reproductions page (https://history.house.gov/About/Rights-and-Reproductions/) concerns only images of objects in the House Collection. Used for verification only, so the deck does not depend on this assessment."@en .

<https://www.whitehouse.gov/administration/donald-j-trump/>
    dcterms:title "The White House: Donald J. Trump (administration page)" ;
    dcterms:creator "The White House" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "https://www.whitehouse.gov/copyright/ — \"Pursuant to federal law, government-produced materials appearing on this site are not copyright protected.\""@en .

<https://www.usa.gov/presidents>
    dcterms:title "Presidents, vice presidents, and first ladies (USAGov)" ;
    dcterms:creator "USAGov, U.S. General Services Administration" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A work of the United States Government (the General Services Administration's USAGov): 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The page states no licence of its own (its Website policies and notices page, https://www.usa.gov/website-policies-and-notices, lists \"Privacy and security policies\", \"Accessibility policy\", \"USA.gov linking policy\", \"How to cite USA.gov\", \"Free commercial downloads\" and \"Paperwork Reduction Act statements\" and states no copyright or licence terms; the older address https://www.usa.gov/website-policies answered 404). Used for verification only."@en .

<https://millercenter.org/president>
    dcterms:title "U.S. Presidents (Miller Center of Public Affairs, University of Virginia)" ;
    dcterms:creator "Miller Center of Public Affairs, University of Virginia" ;
